{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Your brothers shall praise you.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): that he shall be king over them. <br><b>Your father's sons shall bow down to you.</b> It does not say 'your mother's sons,' for there is no need to mention the sons of Leah his mother — but even the sons of Rachel and the sons of the maidservants, all shall bow down to him. And he applied to him 'a lion's whelp,' and it would have been fitting to say 'Judah is a lion,' but he said 'whelp' (גור) because he was still a child. And he called him 'lion' on account of his strength, for the lion is king among beasts and is called mighty (גבור). As it is written (Proverbs 30): ״ליש גבור בבהמה״. And it is said of Judah: ״כי יהודה גבר באחיו״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:25.559011079Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}